     1	#!/usr/bin/env bash
     2	# scripts/tests/test-upgrade-spec-ownership.sh
     3	# PLAN-166 F3 (ADR-155-AMEND-1) — delivery-record ownership of the three
     4	# conditional framework surfaces (SPEC/v1, root PROTOCOL.md,
     5	# .claude/.framework-version) across install → upgrade → doctor → updater.
     6	#
     7	# AC-3 scenarios exercised:
     8	#   S1  maintainer fresh install: SPEC/v1 + PROTOCOL.md + marker DELIVERED
     9	#       and recorded in the baseline manifest; marker == source VERSION;
    10	#       delivered_* ops journaled in .install-state.json
    11	#   S2  2nd-upgrade FORCED route (r6 — the load-bearing fixture): baseline
    12	#       ALREADY contains SPEC/v1 records, SPEC edited locally => upgrade
    13	#       REPLACES it (backup in .claude.bak/<ts>/SPEC/v1) — the generic
    14	#       classified walk would have PRESERVED the edit; root VERSION
    15	#       sentinel is NOT touched (S238/ADR-155 class)
    16	#   S3  user-ceremony install + `upgrade --no-replay` (r9 MANDATORY):
    17	#       neither install nor upgrade creates SPEC/v1 or a root PROTOCOL.md
    18	#       (the ceremony is read by the replay-INDEPENDENT reader)
    19	#   S4  legacy ADOPTER-FORK (r20): baseline without SPEC records (v1.2-and-
    20	#       earlier shape) + locally edited SPEC => PRESERVED in place + named
    21	#       WARNING + forensic snapshot (no pristine fingerprint match)
    22	#   S5  pre-existing marker (r20) AND pre-existing root PROTOCOL.md (r13/
    23	#       r17) on a MAINTAINER install: both EXISTS-skipped => NO delivery
    24	#       record => neither is inventoried as framework-owned; the checker
    25	#       refuses the unrecorded marker and falls back to VERSION; doctor
    26	#       does not flag the adopter's PROTOCOL.md as an orphan
    27	#   S6  updater no-loop regression (r8): post-upgrade tree with stale root
    28	#       VERSION reports the NEW version via the recorded marker
    29	#       (up-to-date, exit 0); stripping the marker record flips it back to
    30	#       the stale VERSION (behind, exit != 0) — proves marker-first is
    31	#       load-bearing, not decorative
    32	#   S7  doctor, user mode (r19): adopter's OWN SPEC/v1 + root PROTOCOL.md
    33	#       are NOT orphan candidates under --strict-orphans (flags resolved
    34	#       from the baseline, not from a ceremony default)
    35	#   S8  doctor, maintainer mode (r9 P2): a stray file inside the DELIVERED
    36	#       SPEC/v1 IS an orphan candidate (positive control — the enumeration
    37	#       does include SPEC when the record says delivered)
    38	#
    39	# The pristine-match branch of the legacy migration (target SPEC/v1 byte-
    40	# identical to a shipped v1.2.0-or-earlier tree) deliberately lives in the
    41	# F4 install-v1.2.0→upgrade e2e (needs real tag content); it is NOT
    42	# duplicated here.
    43	#
    44	# bash 3.2-safe. mktemp -d only (xdist/parallel safe). Exits 0 on success,
